# Build-context hygiene (CC-233).
#
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . /app`, which copies the whole checkout.
# Without this file every image built from a working tree carried the host
# `.venv` (a ~370 MB dead layer — the image rebuilds its own venv on top of
# it), plus tool caches and operator-only files. That is the whole of the
# 413 MB -> 657 MB growth the ticket recorded; the dependency layer itself
# grew 11 MB.
#
# Dagger's build_ai already strips .venv and screenshots; this makes a plain
# `docker build` behave the same way.
.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.logfire
.claude
.vscode
.envrc
screenshots

# Operator-only. Never belongs in an image, whatever built it.
secrets.yml
.env
.env.*
!.env.prod.example
notes.org
notes.org_archive
